    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, you said it 'contradicted the notion of a successful outcome' for those workers. so if we're looking at the actual reality for a factory worker in the rust belt, wouldn't it be more accurate to just call it a failure for them? it feels like calling it 'complex' just glosses over the fact that they actually lost out.",
